;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
*T ==> "gaver1" averages or sums 1d Ufiles f1(x), f2(x), f3(x), ...
*T  labels and x axis are taken from first Ufile read; subsequent
*T  Ufiles are interpolated to this x axis if necessary.  In general
*T  "gaver1" computes "f(x) = 1/W*(w1*f1(x) + w2*f2(x) + ... + wn*fn(x))"
*T  where "W = w1 + w2 + ... + wn".  Because the x axis is taken from
*T  f1, the calculation "f(x) = 0.0*f1(x) + 1.0*f2(x)" actually yields
*T  a remapping of f2 onto the x axis grid of f1.
*T  ...the following demo sums 4 profiles with varying weight...
;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
H ECE PR1 Q
;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
H ECE AVG Q
;GAVER1: ENTER OPCODE (A/D/L/P/R/S/W/X/Q):$
A
;GAVER1: ENTER 5 DIGIT INPUT SHOT # OR "X" TO EXIT INPUT LOOP:$
W
;GAVER1: ENTER 5 DIGIT INPUT SHOT # OR "X" TO EXIT INPUT LOOP:$
37065
;UFSCMP:  ENTER OPCODE (1/2////Q):$
Q
;GAVER1:  ENTER "P" TO PLOT INPUT DATA:$
P
;GRAOPT:  ENTER ONE LETTER OPCODE (.C/A/S/X/Z/G/P/Q):$
Q
;GAVER1:  AVERAGE THIS SHOT? (Y/N):$
Y
;GAVER1:  SPECIFY WEIGHTING FACTOR FOR DATA:$
1
;GAVER1: ENTER 5 DIGIT INPUT SHOT # OR "X" TO EXIT INPUT LOOP:$
F
;GAVER1: ENTER 5 DIGIT INPUT SHOT # OR "X" TO EXIT INPUT LOOP:$
37065
